# Direct dependencies for the sync image, hand-edited.
#
# requirements.txt is GENERATED from this file, constrained by the already
# -compiled backend/requirements.txt so the eight packages both images use
# (asyncpg, croniter, httpx, pydantic-settings, python-dotenv, redis,
# sqlalchemy, structlog) -- and anything transitive underneath them -- land on
# the exact versions backend already pinned, not just versions that happen to
# satisfy both independently. Never hand-edit requirements.txt; regenerate it
# with scripts/compile-requirements.sh. See that script's header for how and
# when, and README.md#dependency-lockfiles for the short version.
#
# Every line below is a package sync_service.py imports or invokes directly.
# Anything pulled in only transitively belongs in requirements.txt, never here.

# Sync service dependencies
asyncpg==0.29.0
sqlalchemy[asyncio]==2.0.25
redis==5.0.1
pydantic-settings==2.1.0
python-dotenv==1.2.3
structlog==24.1.0
croniter==2.0.1
httpx==0.26.0
aiohttp==3.14.3
